SUMMARY:[System Identification & Data-driven Dynamics][Control & Robotics] 
 IFAC SYSID 2027 - Joint journal/conference submission (cutoff time unanno
 unced)
DESCRIPTION:Conference title: IFAC Symposium on System Identification\nWebs
 ite: https://conferences.ifac-control.org/sysid2027/\nSource URL: https:/
 /conferences.ifac-control.org/sysid2027/participate/\nLocation: Lyon\, Fr
 ance\nTopics: System Identification & Data-driven Dynamics\, Control & Ro
 botics\, Time Series & Sequential Data\, Machine Learning\nSize: M\nSubmi
 ssion type: Paper-based\nConfidence: confirmed\nLast checked date: 2026-1
 0-29\nNotes: Triennial TC 1.1 symposium. On 2026-10-29 the participate pa
 ge strikes out Nov 2 and gives Nov 15\, 2026 for conference papers (Oct 1
  to Oct 11 for joint journal papers). The submission system opened 1 June
  2026 (day only\, no time). Deadline days are official\; cutoff hours use
  provisional end-of-day AoE. Size is an editorial category.\nScope: Syste
 m identification and data-driven modeling for dynamical systems and contr
 ol. Characteristic themes include nonlinear identification\, model reduct
 ion\, identification software and benchmarks\, learning across systems\, 
 and dynamic networks. Application tracks remain grounded in identifying o
 r learning dynamical models\, rather than becoming general-purpose domain
  conferences.\nAdditional topics: Nonlinear Dynamics & Chaos\, Complex Sy
 stems & Network Science\nScope sources (2027): https://conferences.ifac-c
 ontrol.org/sysid2027/participate/\nScope last checked: 2026-10-07\nOffici
 al deadline day\; exact cutoff hour/timezone is unannounced. Verify the o
 rganizer's submission portal.
URL:https://conferences.ifac-control.org/sysid2027/participate/
END:VEVENT
